⍝ Quad_EB.tc
⍝ ----------------------------------

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ A ⎕EB B is try/finally: B's result (or error) is the result;
      ⍝ A is the cleanup, always executed after B, its value (if any)
      ⍝ discarded (not displayed). Hence ⎕← to make A's execution
      ⍝ visible. If B fails, )MORE names B's failure.
      ⍝
      '⎕←"CLEAN-UP"' ⎕EB '⍳4.5'
CLEAN-UP
DOMAIN ERROR+
      '⎕←"CLEAN-UP"' ⎕EB '⍳4.5'
      ^

      )MORE
A ⎕EB B: B failed with DOMAIN ERROR in: ⍳4.5

      )SIC
      )ERASE FOO

∇FOO
   '⎕←"CLEAN-UP"' ⎕EB '→L3'
   NOT REACHED
L3: 'GOON'
∇

      FOO
CLEAN-UP
GOON

      )SIC
      )ERASE FOO

∇FOO
   '⎕←"CLEAN-UP"' ⎕EB '→'
   NOT REACHED
∇

      FOO
CLEAN-UP

      )SI

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ Bugs30 #2 (Blake McBride): A containing a →N with no enclosing
      ⍝ defined function used to hang the interpreter forever (→N was
      ⍝ misresolved as a jump to the ⎕EB macro's own line 1, i.e. the
      ⍝ very statement that runs A, looping). Fixed: no enclosing
      ⍝ function means SYNTAX ERROR (like a bare ⍎'→1'), not a hang.

      '→1' ⎕EB '2+2'
SYNTAX ERROR+
      →1
      ^

      )SIC

      '→0' ⎕EB '2+2'
SYNTAX ERROR+
      →0
      ^

      )SIC

      '→¯1' ⎕EB '2+2'
SYNTAX ERROR+
      →¯1
      ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ →N with a real enclosing function must still branch for real.

      )ERASE FOO

∇Z←FOO
      A←'→3' ⎕EB '2+2'
      Z←100
      Z←999
∇

      FOO
999

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      )ERASE FOO

      ⍝ result rules (try/finally):
      ⍝
      ⍝   B       A       result of A ⎕EB B
      ⍝   value   value   B's value (A's value discarded, not displayed)
      ⍝   error   value   B's error  ()MORE: B's failure)
      ⍝   value   error   A's error
      ⍝   error   error   A's error  ()MORE: B's failure)
      ⍝
      ⍝ A may have no value at all (e.g. a cleanup function without
      ⍝ result, or an empty A).
      ⍝
      )ERASE CLEANUP
∇CLEANUP
 '... CLEANUP ran'
∇

      Z←'5' ⎕EB '2+2'
      Z
4

      '5' ⎕EB '2+2'
4

      'CLEANUP' ⎕EB '2+2'
... CLEANUP ran
4

      '' ⎕EB '2+2'
4

      ')WSID' ⎕EB '2+2'
4

      '5' ⎕EB '3÷0'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      '5' ⎕EB '3÷0'
      ^

      )MORE
A ⎕EB B: B failed with DOMAIN ERROR in: 3÷0

      )SIC
      '1÷0' ⎕EB '2+2'
DOMAIN ERROR
      1÷0
      ^^

      )SIC
      '1÷0' ⎕EB '3÷0'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      1÷0
      ^^

      )MORE
A ⎕EB B: B failed with DOMAIN ERROR in: 3÷0

      )SIC

      ⍝ a ⎕EC inside B is not ⎕EB's own ⎕EC: no )MORE for it.
      ⍝
      '' ⎕EB '↑⎕EC ''3÷0'''
0

      )MORE
NO )MORE ERROR INFO

      )ERASE CLEANUP

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #7) -- CLOSED AS NOT A BUG
      ⍝ (2026-10-02, after discussion with the user): an SI-modifying
      ⍝ command as the A operand, e.g. ')OFF' ⎕EB '2+2', really executes
      ⍝ (and ends the session), whereas the same command as B gives the
      ⍝ ⎕EC guard's DOMAIN ERROR. That asymmetry is intended: ⎕EB is
      ⍝ try/finally -- B is the protected expression, run under ⎕EC
      ⍝ (which must return a result for B, hence the guard), and A is
      ⍝ the cleanup expression, ⍎'d unguarded AFTER B whether B
      ⍝ succeeded or not, so that A is guaranteed to be at least
      ⍝ attempted. ')OFF' ⎕EB B ("whatever happens in B, end the session
      ⍝ afterwards") is a legitimate request; vetoing it would break the
      ⍝ very guarantee ⎕EB exists for. Same reasoning as ⎕EA's A operand
      ⍝ (see Quad_EA.tc, Bugs31 #7). As with a C++ finally block that
      ⍝ calls exit(), B's own outcome (result or error) is then lost.
      ⍝
      ⍝ Blake's )SAVE claim (a "*" )SI frame saved into the workspace)
      ⍝ reproduces, but identically for a plain ⍎')SAVE ...' without
      ⍝ ⎕EB -- see Quad_EA.tc; it is )SAVE's own frame handling.
      ⍝
      ⍝ )OFF/)CLEAR/)SAVE can't be run for real in this shared-process
      ⍝ suite; )SIC takes the identical E_COMMAND_PUSHED path and is
      ⍝ safe here. It must reach Command.cc silently (no DOMAIN ERROR);
      ⍝ the whole ⎕EB statement never completes, so B's result (4) is
      ⍝ not displayed either -- same as a plain ⍎')SIC' would.
      ⍝
      ')SIC' ⎕EB '2+2'
      )SI

      )CHECK
OK      - no stale functions
OK      - no stale values
OK      - no stale indices
OK      - no duplicate parents

      ⍝ ==================================

